meta {
  name: AI Usage
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/me/ai-usage
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  GET /api/me/ai-usage — what you have spent and how much is left, so a client
  can show the ceiling rather than discovering it by hitting it.

  Three figures, all in micro-dollars (millionths of a dollar, as integers).
  chat covers asking questions, indexing covers embedding your notes as you
  write them, and global is everyone's combined ceiling — which exists because
  per-user limits bound one person, not the bill.

  The window rolls rather than resetting, so resetsAt is a full window from now
  rather than a fixed hour. A calendar reset would let the whole allowance be
  spent either side of midnight.
}
